# nr-relay-twin-perf

## Cargo and workspace edits

File: native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/Cargo.toml. Anchor: the `[[test]]` blocks (after `name = "twin"`). Add:

```toml
[[test]]
name = "twin_perf"
path = "tests/twin_perf.rs"
required-features = ["test-support"]
```

Without it the target is built without the `test-support` feature, `relay_twin_host` is not built and
`env!("CARGO_BIN_EXE_relay_twin_host")` in tests/twin/proc.rs does not resolve.

No new crate: base64, futures, serde_json, sha2, tokio (rt, rt-multi-thread, net, time, io-util, sync, macros),
tokio-tungstenite (handshake) and mixdog-rt are dependencies of mixdog-relay already; mixdog-testkit and tempfile are its
dev-dependencies. Cargo.lock: no change.

compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING: no name is added or removed by this task.

## Run

`cargo nextest run -p mixdog-relay --release --features test-support --offline -E 'binary(twin_perf)' --run-ignored only --success-output immediate`
(see tests/twin_perf/README.md). The three unit tests of load.rs, and the two of twin_perf.rs that pin the verdict and the
median, run without `--run-ignored`.
